@lang pt
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cp-dominio`
IMPORT `cp-pena`
IMPORT `cp-g1c-comum`

-- Código Penal, Parte Geral, Título VIII — arts. 109 a 119: a prescrição.
-- Written by g1c. Arts. 107, 108 and 120 are in
-- cp-g1c-extincao-da-punibilidade.l4.
--
-- THE TEXT ENCODED is Planalto's compilation: arts. 109–119 as re-enacted by
-- Lei nº 7.209/1984, with art. 109 caput and VI and art. 110, § 1º in the
-- wording of Lei nº 12.234/2010 (§ 2º revoked by it); art. 111, V in that of
-- Lei nº 14.344/2022; art. 114 in that of Lei nº 9.268/1996; art. 115 in that
-- of Lei nº 15.160/2025; art. 116, II–IV in that of Lei nº 13.964/2019; art.
-- 117, IV in that of Lei nº 11.596/2007, and V–VI in that of Lei nº
-- 9.268/1996. Prescription is penal law: a harsher later wording does not
-- reach an earlier crime (fork F-g1c-19). So, by the date of the crime:
--   * art. 109, VI (three years, formerly less) and art. 110, § 1º refuse
--     for a crime before Lei nº 12.234/2010;
--   * art. 111, V refuses for a crime before Lei nº 14.344/2022;
--   * art. 115 refuses for every crime before Lei nº 15.160/2025, and every
--     prescription with it (conductor's ruling, 2026-09-30);
--   * art. 116, III and IV (added) do not suspend for a crime before Lei nº
--     13.964/2019, and a suspension under II (re-worded) refuses;
--   * an interruption under art. 117, IV refuses for a crime before Lei nº
--     11.596/2007, and one under V or VI for a crime before Lei nº
--     9.268/1996.
-- The dates are in § `As vigências`; notes/g1c.md says which were confirmed.
--
-- EVERY PERIOD IS COUNTED BY ART. 10 through `o último dia do prazo`: the
-- first day counts, and the period has run from the day after its last day.
-- A suspension (art. 116) adds its days to the running period; an
-- interruption (art. 117) starts the whole period again from its own day
-- (§ 2º), except the start of serving (V), which stops it.
--
-- THE "PENA EM ABSTRATO" (art. 109): the maximum of the preceito secundário
-- with the case's causes of increase at their largest fraction and of
-- decrease at their smallest — `a pena cominada com as causas` (cp-pena, PLAN
-- § 2.3). The increase for a crime continuado is not one of those causes
-- (Súmula 497 STF, fork F-sweep-a-05, in g1b's register since art. 71 is
-- its lowest-numbered provision); nor is an aggravating circumstance.
--
-- SWEEP ENTRIES ACTED ON HERE: M-sweep-a-06 (Tema 788: art. 112, I without
-- "para a acusação", in two arms, binding), M-sweep-a-15 (F-sweep-a-05),
-- M-sweep-a-32 (F-sweep-a-17), M-sweep-a-33 (F-sweep-a-18), M-sweep-a-34
-- (F-sweep-a-19); M-sweep-a-17 and M-sweep-a-35 are confirmed by the text as
-- encoded (art. 110, § 1º computes on the penalty applied, and only on one
-- the sentence has fixed), M-sweep-a-26 is a rule of proof (the age is an
-- input), and M-sweep-a-36 and -37 are the sweep's scoped-out entries.
--
-- Forks: F-g1c-25 (art. 114: the fine cominated or applied), F-g1c-26 (art.
-- 115's "sentença"), F-g1c-27 (art. 111, V: whose age), F-g1c-28 (art. 110,
-- § 1º: the date of the denúncia), F-g1c-29 (suspended days added as days),
-- F-g1c-30 (art. 117, VI: the day of the reincidência), and the four the
-- sweep reserved: F-sweep-a-17, -18, -19 (F-sweep-a-05 is g1b's, cross-referred).

§ `Título VIII — Da extinção da punibilidade`

§§ `Arts. 109 a 119 — Da prescrição`

§§§ `As vigências`

